  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+2, & x<1 \\\\ 3, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5}^{1}(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x){|}_{-5}^{1}+3x{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(1)^{2}}{2}+2(1)-\\frac{(-5)^{2}}{2}-2(-5)]+[3(3)-3(1)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}+2-\\frac{25}{2}+10]+[9-3] \\\\  & =0+6 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
